body:
Agent-guide reference file: each kalide author guide is delivered to a project as a kalide-owned full guide file plus a short pointer file that names it. The full guide is `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` at the project root (the deck guide, agent-authoring, for a deck) or the library root (the library guide, library-agent-guide, for a template library). The pointer is the project's own `AGENTS.md`, whose content is the single line `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md` (under a short header when the file is created).

The pointer rule is idempotent and author-preserving:
- `AGENTS.md` absent: it is created carrying the reference (with a short header);
- `AGENTS.md` present and already containing the exact string `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md`: it is left byte-for-byte untouched;
- `AGENTS.md` present without that string: the reference line is appended and the author's existing content is byte-preserved.

Appending the reference line to a present author `AGENTS.md` is the one permitted modification of that file; `AGENTS.md` content is never otherwise rewritten by scaffolding. The full guide is written only when `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is absent (an existing `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is kalide-owned and brought forward by `kalide upgrade`, upgrade-refresh-owned-scaffold). Both files are text-only, offline, inert to load/validate/render/serve/list, and not template assets (global.constraint.no-embedded-template-assets, solution.constraint.agent-guide-unbranded-inert).

AC:
- immediately after any scaffolding command, `<root>/AGENTS_KALIDE.md` holds the full guide and `<root>/AGENTS.md` contains the string `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md`;
- a project whose `AGENTS.md` already contains the string is left byte-for-byte unchanged by a further scaffolding or upgrade run;
- a project whose `AGENTS.md` is author content without the string gains the appended reference line, with all its other bytes unchanged;
- neither file is read by `kalide start` or `kalide templates`: a project holding both loads, validates, renders, serves and lists unchanged.
